  "ownerStatements": [
    {
      "id": "41d5797f-d115-4cce-90fd-8ccc835b86cb",
      "text": "Prepare a set of directions for CODEX for the Unity Game Engine development"
    },
    {
      "id": "7c6cc02d-a5b6-4d38-822e-6565dfd8f1be",
      "text": "The rules engine alone requires AI oversight we both know that"
    },
    {
      "id": "b65567ca-8093-4aa2-97f2-059d325b4e88",
      "text": "when you write this, I know when I publish it, there is growing hatred on AI but I dont have millions to develop a game nor do I have the years of game development experience to bring this forward."
    },
    {
      "id": "b4c25f09-07df-4625-aa51-d2403189d8aa",
      "text": "How would the game engine look?"
    },
    {
      "id": "374b7d9e-41fd-42a4-934e-711ad616b4b9",
      "text": "I would love a full 3d rendition MMO style game but I know that is technically impossible with CODEX. What I am planning is a SNES Style CRPG with 3 base games.\n\nThe exploration, Tactical, Resource Management.\n\nExploration-self explanatory. I was thinking free control like Secret of Mana where you can run and Jump, use simple mapped commands to explore, dig, mark, open chest doors etc.\n\nTactical.\nTrue CRPG (think owlcat)\n\nResource Management,\nWhere you can hit all the crafting and research systems, send ai partnerrs to do certain tasks, (fishing, mining, farming etc)"
    }
  ],
  "ownerEstablishedProductDirection": [
    "Unity engine",
    "SNES-style CRPG",
    "Direct-control exploration with run/jump/contextual explore/dig/mark/open interactions",
    "Tactical CRPG experience; Owlcat comparison does not independently replace existing cadence",
    "Resource management with crafting, research and companion tasks; fishing/mining/farming examples",
    "Ongoing AI-assisted rules-engine and engineering oversight"
  ],
